==Strategy==
[[Sunrise Doge]] is a metal enemy, so use fast critical hitters like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Jurassic Cat]] or, better, [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]] to defeat it as soon as possible, as to avoid dealing with him and more than one Tiger Doge at once. The Tiger Doges can be easily defeated with [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher]] units, most preferably [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]; who, at level 30, can one-shot every enemy consistently. However, on Level 10, the Tiger Doges can actually survive from a level 30 Awakened Bahamut's first hit.

To stall the enemies, bring many meatshields and/or a good staller for traitless ([[Suntan Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Suntan]], [[Healer (Special Cat)|Healer Cat]] etc.). [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] is also useful, but gets shredded too quickly in the last stages.

When it comes to attackers, [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]] shines the most, but it is easy enough to win by just stacking any midranger with area attack, such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman]], as long as they don't cost too much.

A good strategy that will easily beat Level 10 is equip 7-8 spammable cheap meatshields, and Awakened Bahamut Cat. Cat CPU and Rich Cat are recommended. When you enter battle, save up around 4500 cents. Spam a bit of meatshields so Bahamut doesn't rush forward and die, then buy Awakened Bahamut. Turn on CPU, and sit back while your meatshields shred through Angry Sun.

